#=GF RN [1]
#=GF RM 15220462
#=GF RT The 3' cis-acting genomic replication element of the severe acute
#=GF RT respiratory syndrome coronavirus can function in the murine coronavirus
#=GF RT genome.
#=GF RA Goebel SJ, Taylor J, Masters PS
#=GF RL J Virol. 2004;78:7846-7851.
#=GF RN [2]
#=GF RM 25736566
#=GF RT The structure and functions of coronavirus genomic 3' and 5' ends.
#=GF RA Yang D, Leibowitz JL
#=GF RL Virus Res. 2015;206:120-133.
#=GF RN [3]
#=GF RM 21378501
#=GF RT RNA-RNA and RNA-protein interactions in coronavirus replication and
#=GF RT transcription.
#=GF RA Sola I, Mateos-Gomez PA, Almazan F, Zuniga S, Enjuanes L
#=GF RL RNA Biol. 2011;8:237-248.
#=GF RN [4]
#=GF RM 27712622
#=GF RT Coronavirus cis-Acting RNA Elements.
#=GF RA Madhugiri R, Fricke M, Marz M, Ziebuhr J
#=GF RL Adv Virus Res. 2016;96:127-163.
#=GF CC The 3' UTR of betacoronaviruses is approximately 300-500 nucleotides long.
#=GF CC The most 5' structure is the bulged stem-loop (BSL), starting downstream
#=GF CC of the N gene stop codon and is essential for viral replication. It is
#=GF CC predicted to be conserved among betacoronaviruses. Downstream to the BSL
#=GF CC lies the hypervariable bulged-stemloop region (HVR), containing a triple
#=GF CC helix junction. The hairpin stem-loop arising from this junction
#=GF CC participates in the pseudoknot pairing with the BSL region. The pseudoknot
#=GF CC and the BSL partially overlap and therefore cannot be formed at the same
#=GF CC time. It is proposed that the BSL and pseudoknot act as a molecular switch
#=GF CC that may regulate a transition during viral RNA synthesis. Part of the HVR
#=GF CC is the octanucleotide sequence '5-GGAAGAGC-3' which is conserved among
#=GF CC alpha- and betacoronaviruses.
#=GF WK Coronavirus_3'_UTR
#=GF SQ 17

